## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Reckons.AI Docs - Why Reckons.AI
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## The positioning graph. What the enterprise semantic-layer vendors sell, what it
## costs, and what is left when you remove the invoice.
##
## This file is persuasion, and says so. static/reckons-competitive.ttl exists to learn
## from the neighbourhood and refuses to score points; this one is aimed at a reader
## deciding whether to care. What it inherits from that file is the standard of evidence
## rather than the neutrality. Every figure is sourced and dated, and every limitation of
## ours sits in the same paragraph as the claim it weakens.
##
## House style for this file, which differs from the older graphs on purpose. No shouting:
## emphasis is carried by sentence structure, not by capitalised words. Em dashes are
## rationed to roughly one per paragraph. These pages are read by people deciding whether
## this product is for them, and the older convention reads as a memo to ourselves.
##
## Children of the four topic hubs carry kpred:render-inline, so they compose into a few
## substantial pages instead of nineteen thin ones. See earnsPage in scripts/docs-pages.ts.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## A claim this page must never make
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Do not write that the enterprise products came after Reckons.AI, or that they copied
## this methodology. Checked on 2026-09-16 and false: our first commit is 2026-06-09, the
## OntoBricks repository was created 2026-04-07 and released v0.1.1 on 2026-04-23, and
## Fabric IQ was announced at Ignite 2025. Palantir, Stardog and Ontotext predate us by
## years to decades.
##
## The evidence is kept as knowledge in static/reckons-roadmap.ttl under F205
## kpred:measured, and is deliberately not published. A reader needs the argument, not our
## editing history. The page leads with convergence instead, which is both true and
## stronger.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

